  <h3 class="linklist">Bolex Reporter, Volume 16</h3>
  <!-- EPHEMERA and bolex reporter stuff -->
  <div id="books"> 
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltright" src="../images/reporter/16_1.jpg" alt="Bolex Reporter" width="220" height="282"></li>
      <li class="bolrep">1966</li>
      <li class="bolrep">Volume 16, Number 1</li>
      <li class="repart"><strong>Articles:</strong> "The Avant Garde Cinema", 
        Peter Vanadia; "Twice a Man", Gregory J. Markopoulos; "The New American 
        Cinema Group", Fred W. McDarrah; "Techniques", Maurice Amar; "Film and 
        the New Dance", Ann Halprin; "What To Do With Your Film", Geza de Rosner; 
        "Films for Television", Jim Doney; "What Makes a Good Travelogue?", Martin 
        A. Forrest; "An Unusual Documentary", Edgar J. Thompson; "Grand Canyon 
        Passage", Merton J. Goldsmith; "A Close-up of Nature", P.T. Fetko; "Surfing 
        World-wide", Bruce Brown; "Wildlife", Cartl E. Scott and John E. Swedberg; 
        "Arctic Voyage", Robert W.F. Cundy</li>
      <li class="desc">The previous two issues were devoted mainly to the discussion 
        of professional uses of Bolex cameras in commerce, industry and education. 
        In the 3rd and final 'Professional Issue', the use of Bolex cameras in 
        the arts is discussed. "The New American Cinema Group", profiles some 
        of the film-makers of the Avant Garde and underground cinema: Peter Goldman, 
        Marie Menken, Naomi Levine, Ken Jacobs, Stan Vanderbeek, Gregory Markopoulos, 
        Robert Breer, Robert Frank, David Brooks, Jack Smith, Buddy Wirtschaefter, 
        Jerry Malanga, Andy Warhol and Jonas Mekas.</li>
      <li class="pp">36 pages</li>
    </ul>
    <hr>
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltleft" src="../images/reporter/donthave.jpg" alt="Missing Issue!" width="220" height="284"></li>
